From: Wisp contributors
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apollo5x: let an application replace soc_early_init_hook

Wisp's hardware images (rung4.md W25) run their own SoC start-up behind the Even bootloader and
Wisp Boot instead of the HAL's low-power init, SIMO buck enable and temperature update: the
weak attribute lets the app's strong definition win. Builds without one are unchanged.

diff --git a/soc/ambiq/apollo5x/soc.c b/soc/ambiq/apollo5x/soc.c
index 8cdf144c..c0a9b6a0 100644
--- a/soc/ambiq/apollo5x/soc.c
+++ b/soc/ambiq/apollo5x/soc.c
@@ -283,7 +283,7 @@ void ambiq_apollo510b_ble_lp_runtime_init(void)
 }
 #endif
 
-void soc_early_init_hook(void)
+__weak void soc_early_init_hook(void)
 {
 	/* Enable Loop and branch info cache */
 	SCB->CCR |= SCB_CCR_LOB_Msk;
